 # Budgeted Gaussian Splatting
-
-
 ## Overview
-Budgeted Gaussian Splatting (BCT) is a training and deployment method for large-scale 3D Gaussian Splatting that enables variable primitive counts (Level of Detail) without retraining, using a continuous budget-quality curve to select primitives [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [CityGaussian / VastGaussian / DoGaussian](6143-citygaussian-vastgaussian-dogaussian.md) and [Octree-GS](7341-octree-gs.md) by decoupling the LOD selection from the training process, allowing a single trained model to be exported to any standard rasterizer with different budgets, achieving near-lossless quality at low compression ratios [S1, unofficial].
-
